      "writtenOn": "2019-08-23T07:47:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you think about this:\n\n1. Add a function in intel_x86.c intel_x86_power_signal_interrupt() which looks something like this:\n\nvoid intel_x86_power_signal_interrupt(enum gpio_signal signal)\n{\n    intel_x86_handle_rsmrst_assertion();\n    power_signal_interrupt(signal);\n}\n\n2. Change gpio.inc for any board that requires rsmrst assertion to be quick to use intel_x86_power_signal_interrupt() instead of power_signal_interrupt().\n\nReason for suggesting this:\n\n1. It avoids having to add another config option. This is under the assumption that we have linker options enabled to garbage collect unused functions.\n2. It avoids having to put intel_x86 specific call back in power/common.c i.e intel_x86_handle_rsmrst_assertion().\n3. This also gives you the flexibility to use intel_x86_handle_rsmrst_assertion() only for PG_EC_RSMRST_L in gpio.inc i.e. when other power signals change you do not have to spend any time looking at the GPIO states for rsmrst_in and rsmrst_out.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 697,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 697,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "cc9168d26b8b5095ecb674f0053115799d7f2d6b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
